<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila silvestris Turing wavenumber at 2.995 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 89.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the pass-1 readout, mask, and terminal-frame gaps. Power-weighted spectral centroids track the dispersion curve with Pearson r = 0.9981 (wavenumber) and 0.9972 (wavelength), RMSE 0.208 µm. The dorsal wing-band mask keeps 17 dark islands (the raw dark mask had 139). The GIF has 12 frames at 720x576; its last frame is the Kilohana voucher, and computer-vision similarity against that photograph is 96.0 with last-frame orientation KS 0.012. Equal diffusion remains stable. k_this/k_serrata = 30.80 and k_this/k_simulans = 27.57 at age 0 Ma. The 2.995 µm wavelength is the assigned detail tier, not a measurement from Carson & Bryant (1979) and not an identification of the photographed wing spots (Gompel et al. 2005). Overall 89.6/100 (faithfulness 89.1, reproducibility 90.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0dc967f22ddaa01ca809b3701e8da57313f6c44d; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, Pillow, matplotlib. Signing profile absent.. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0dc967f22ddaa01ca809b3701e8da57313f6c44d, image/png, 594499 B, 1248×984 px, artifact_sha256 0830930fc3e69be615317c86b3b6990518c90e2e1cecc6399d8126140993dfe5 (sha256 0830930fc3e69be615317c86b3b6990518c90e2e1cecc6399d8126140993dfe5), spec_fingerprint 94f67ddc05494c16449850f8c780e88f2c89119a3224682e596b88bad888be9c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 94f67ddc05494c16449850f8c780e88f2c89119a3224682e596b88bad888be9c; artifact_sha256: 0830930fc3e69be615317c86b3b6990518c90e2e1cecc6399d8126140993dfe5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=9f4f77b1d9bee8df..., datasets/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=dd93694218361504..., datasets/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4ff27448f5d20b31...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | Carson & Bryant (1979): 20-30 extra tibial cilia in northeast males; absent in D. heteroneura. Spiess & Carson (1981) tested courtship discrimination. Carson (1982) places the species on the young Hawaiian volcanoes. | Gompel et al. (2005): macroscopic wing pigment patterns in Drosophila are cis-regulatory.; reconstructed_in_script: lambda_c = 2.995e-6 m at gamma = 1, d = D_v/D_u = 20, on a patch of eight wavelengths. Predecessor contrast d = 8 at 92.26 µm; successor contrast d = 10 at 82.56 µm. Those ratios are defined in this slot. | Pass-2 measurements: centroid sweep, size-filtered wing-band components, equal-diffusion ablation, and the nonlinear onset wavenumber ratio.; transfer_boundary: Results are for this detail-tier wavenumber on D. silvestris. They do not identify the mechanism of picture-wing spots, tibial cilia rows, or the patterns of D. serrata and D. simulans.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Kilohana photograph is a 3 µm reaction-diffusion pattern. The terminal GIF frame is the voucher so the animal can be scored; the wavelength law is the dispersion relation. | Does not claim an independent second assessor or a signed nanopublication. No nanopub profile was available, and scores were not invented to hide that. | Does not claim the gallery phrase '100+ tibial courtship cilia rows'. The paper's count is 20-30 extra cilia between two rows.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R5 (open). No independent second assessor has scored this audit.",
        "remediation needed: R6 (open). The wing-spot mask is a luminance and size heuristic (17 components), not a homologised spot map.",
        "remediation needed: R7 (open). Wavelength RMSE is 0.208 µm because the Fourier lattice is discrete even after the centroid.",
        "remediation needed: R8 (open). Nanopublications are unsigned: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent. Do not treat the TriG as signed." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.96e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
