<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila silvestris Turing wavenumber at 2.995 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Drosophila silvestris)",
        "Drosophila silvestris Turing wavenumber at 2.995 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila silvestris morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila silvestris specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila silvestris" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim an independent second assessor or a signed nanopublication. No nanopub profile was available, and scores were not invented to hide that.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the Kilohana photograph is a 3 µm reaction-diffusion pattern. The terminal GIF frame is the voucher so the animal can be scored; the wavelength law is the dispersion relation.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the gallery phrase '100+ tibial courtship cilia rows'. The paper's count is 20-30 extra cilia between two rows.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass-2 measurements: centroid sweep, size-filtered wing-band components, equal-diffusion ablation, and the nonlinear onset wavenumber ratio.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: lambda_c = 2.995e-6 m at gamma = 1, d = D_v/D_u = 20, on a patch of eight wavelengths. Predecessor contrast d = 8 at 92.26 µm; successor contrast d = 10 at 82.56 µm. Those ratios are defined in this slot.",
        "reported_in_source: Carson & Bryant (1979): 20-30 extra tibial cilia in northeast males; absent in D. heteroneura. Spiess & Carson (1981) tested courtship discrimination. Carson (1982) places the species on the young Hawaiian volcanoes.",
        "reported_in_source: Gompel et al. (2005): macroscopic wing pigment patterns in Drosophila are cis-regulatory.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics.",
        "transfer_boundary: Results are for this detail-tier wavenumber on D. silvestris. They do not identify the mechanism of picture-wing spots, tibial cilia rows, or the patterns of D. serrata and D. simulans." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila silvestris (Hawaiian Big-Island Giant Picture-Wing Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila silvestris; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, Pillow, matplotlib. Signing profile absent.; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | Carson & Bryant (1979): 20-30 extra tibial cilia in northeast males; absent in D. heteroneura. Spiess & Carson (1981) tested courtship discrimination. Carson (1982) places the species on the young Hawaiian volcanoes. | Gompel et al. (2005): macroscopic wing pigment patterns in Drosophila are cis-regulatory.; reconstructed_in_script: lambda_c = 2.995e-6 m at gamma = 1, d = D_v/D_u = 20, on a patch of eight wavelengths. Predecessor contrast d = 8 at 92.26 µm; successor contrast d = 10 at 82.56 µm. Those ratios are defined in this slot. | Pass-2 measurements: centroid sweep, size-filtered wing-band components, equal-diffusion ablation, and the nonlinear onset wavenumber ratio.; transfer_boundary: Results are for this detail-tier wavenumber on D. silvestris. They do not identify the mechanism of picture-wing spots, tibial cilia rows, or the patterns of D. serrata and D. simulans.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Kilohana photograph is a 3 µm reaction-diffusion pattern. The terminal GIF frame is the voucher so the animal can be scored; the wavelength law is the dispersion relation. | Does not claim an independent second assessor or a signed nanopublication. No nanopub profile was available, and scores were not invented to hide that. | Does not claim the gallery phrase '100+ tibial courtship cilia rows'. The paper's count is 20-30 extra cilia between two rows.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
